WHAT THIS COVERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

Covered (original work in this project): the Python modules at the top level
and in common/, dashboard/, evaluation/, exploration/, reporting/, rewards/,
training/, tools/ and tests/; dashboard/web/ (except dashboard/web/static/
vendor/); docs/ and the other documentation and configuration files; and the
trained model files glitch_hunter_main_brain.zip and
glitch_hunter_main_brain_coverage.npz.

Not covered - someone else's work, under its own terms (see
docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md):
  games/mario_clean/ and games/mario_bugged/   the Super Mario Bros clone
                          and its assets (upstream carries no license)
  dashboard/web/static/vendor/   the Socket.IO client (MIT) and the
                          Press Start 2P font (SIL Open Font License 1.1)
  the game's graphics, music and sounds wherever they appear, including the
  screenshots in docs/assets/ and in every incident report (Nintendo)

Nothing here gives you any right to those parts. The line above only says
that this notice does not claim them.

Versions of this project that were published earlier under the MIT License
remain available under those terms to those who already received them; this
notice applies to this version and to every later one.
